id: E2622
draft: true
title: Pure resource CMake packages need path-preserving Conan consumers
severity: 2
category: conan|cmake|resource-package|consumer-test
match_keywords: CMake install data tree, CMAKE_INSTALL_DATADIR, Ogg resource package, non-empty file consumer, data-only Conan package
symptom: A Debian data package has no library dependency or upstream test suite, and a generic Conan package check can pass while omitting the installed resource tree or changing its relative paths.
root_cause: Resource packages are validated by filesystem contracts rather than linkable APIs. CMake's full data directory is computed from the install prefix, so a recipe that does not bind CMAKE_INSTALL_DATADIR can place resources outside the expected package layout. A test that only checks package creation does not prove that consumers can locate representative data.
fix: Use the official archive hash, configure CMake with an explicit data directory, install through the upstream CMake target, preserve relative paths, and add an independent consumer script that checks the resource root, a count threshold, representative files, and non-empty bytes.
verification: conan create archives/l/lomiri-sounds/25.01 -pr:h=<ohos-profile> -pr:b=<windows-profile>; run test_package/test_resources.py against the package folder; verify the full resource inventory and package paths.
scope: Conan recipes for CMake projects whose deliverables are data, themes, sounds, schemas, or other non-linkable files.
safety_boundary: File-presence checks do not establish audio playback or target-device integration. Keep target runtime validation separate, and do not infer a release binary from a local data-only package.
source_event: lomiri-sounds/25.01 adaptation, Issue #2622
source_pr: https://gitcode.com/OpenHarmonyPCDeveloper/build_in_harmonyos/issues/2622
source_commit: pending
